dth: 50%; \"> 3. Observation and Scope </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Unit of observation </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Each row represents one county and its rural public transporation access </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Population or objects represented </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Counties, airports, bus stops, and rail facilities </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Time period covered </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> 2006, 2012, 2018, and 2021 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Geographic area coverage </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Rural block groups in the United States </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 4. Variables and Data Structure </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Main variables/fields </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> State, County, Land Area, Water Area, Population, Year, % Rural Access to Airport/Bus Stop/Rail Station </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Data types included </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Location, numerical, categorical, date, ID </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Direct measurements </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> County population, transportation facility location, year </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Possible proxy variables </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> % Rural Access to Airport/Bus Stop/Rail Station, Household income, Vehicles per household, Civilian labor force </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 5. Documentation </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Documentation found </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Methodology, metadata (column descriptions) </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Stated collection details </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Airport data gotten from FAA's enplanement data and BTS' Office of Airline Administration airport summary; Intercity bus stop data gotten from Greyhound, Amtrak, BTS' June 2005 Rural Scheduled Intercity Transportation and the U.S. Rural Population report, BTS' IPCD, and BTS' Intercity Bus Atlas; Intercity rail facility data gotten from BTS' Febuary 2011 U.S. Rural Population and Scheduled Intercity Transportation in 2010 report, BTS' IPCD, BTS' National Transportation Atlas Database, and Alaska railroad website; Population data gotten from the U.S. Census Bureau and American Community Survey </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n",
